# CCTV wire-format vectors are byte-exact reference data. Git's content sniffing
# classifies most of them as text, and with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default) it rewrites their LF endings to CRLF on checkout, corrupting the
# vectors. That is not hypothetical: it made 61 of 143 vectors fail on Windows
# and was reported upstream as pscheid92/AgeSharp#3.
#
# `-text` disables EOL conversion in both directions. Preferred over `binary`,
# which expands to `-diff -merge -text` and would also suppress diffs on the
# armored vectors, which are human-readable and worth seeing in review.
* -text
